ess the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-9{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375254 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375255 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375256 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375257 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375258 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1041 "selection" 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375255 13194139535936 true] [17592186375253 1110 #uuid "bc2a58bb-1168-5cdf-b886-8365a63eaac6" 13194139535936 true] [17592186375254 1034 "B={\\,}" 13194139535936 true] [17592186375254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535936 true] [17592186375254 1111 #uuid "33e54a05-b2f0-5115-bda0-5e61d7daa6a9" 13194139535936 true] [17592186375255 1034 "B={[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139535936 true] [17592